+The transfer function $T(n)$ maps density $n$ to color and opacity contributions [S1]:
 $$T(n) = \frac{h}{w} \exp \left[ -0.5 \left( \frac{\log_{10} n - \log_{10} n_0}{\sigma} \right)^2 \right]$$
-During ray marching, the per-step color and opacity contribution is computed as $\Delta \mathbf{C} = T(n) \Delta s \cdot h$ and $\Delta \alpha = T(n) \Delta s$ [S1]. These are accumulated using front-to-back compositing: $\mathbf{C}_{out} = \mathbf{C}_{in} + (1 - \alpha_{in}) \Delta \mathbf{C}$ and $\alpha_{out} = \alpha_{in} + (1 - \alpha_{in}) \Delta \alpha$ [G].
